<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Songs in History</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Songs of the age of revolutions</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 20 songs of the age of revolutions in Songs in History: when and where they were made, what they say and how they sound.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/songs/?e=revolutions">Open the songs &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the songs from 1 (the oldest) to 6 (the newest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>La Marseillaise</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Gaudeamus igitur</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Argentine National Anthem</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Amazing Grace</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>O Come, All Ye Faithful</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Marcha Real</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right place next to each song. Their pages will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Mo Li Hua</li><li>Poland Is Not Yet Lost</li><li>Auld Lang Syne</li><li>La Marseillaise</li><li>O Come, All Ye Faithful</li><li>Amazing Grace</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Scotland, United Kingdom</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Jiangnan region (around Suzhou, Shanghai and Hangzhou), China</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Reggio Emilia, Italy</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Strasbourg, France</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Olney, Buckinghamshire, England</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>France, where John Francis Wade lived in exile</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Read the words of <b>O Come, All Ye Faithful</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Read the words of <b>Yankee Doodle</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one song and listen to its performance. Which instruments or voices do you hear, and how does the music fit the words?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Songs travel: find a song on these pages that was sung far from where it was made, or that gave its tune to another song. How did it travel?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/songs/?e=revolutions. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Songs of the age of revolutions</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>O Come, All Ye Faithful <span>1751</span></li><li>Marcha Real <span>1761</span></li><li>Amazing Grace <span>1773</span></li><li>Gaudeamus igitur <span>1781</span></li><li>La Marseillaise <span>1792</span></li><li>Argentine National Anthem <span>1813</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Mo Li Hua <span>2: Jiangnan region (around Suzhou, Shanghai and Hangzhou), China</span></li><li>Poland Is Not Yet Lost <span>3: Reggio Emilia, Italy</span></li><li>Auld Lang Syne <span>1: Scotland, United Kingdom</span></li><li>La Marseillaise <span>4: Strasbourg, France</span></li><li>O Come, All Ye Faithful <span>6: France, where John Francis Wade lived in exile</span></li><li>Amazing Grace <span>5: Olney, Buckinghamshire, England</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers quote the song pages.</p></section></div></details>
